<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conan IV, Duke of Brittany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1138–<a href="/years/1171">1171</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conan IV was duke of Brittany from 1156 to 1166 and earl of Richmond in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a>, he gave up power in 1166 and betrothed his daughter and heiress Constance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s son Geoffrey, bringing Brittany into the Angevin sphere. He kept only the county of Guingamp and died in 1171.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conan-iv-duke-of-brittany.jpg" alt="Conan IV, Duke of Brittany" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dom Morice · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conan_IV_de_Bretagne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Brittany’s position between the Angevin and Capetian worlds drew it into their wars, and Henry II of England forced Duke <b>Conan IV</b> to surrender power in 1166.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Duchy of Brittany · Military</a></li></ul></section>
